prop:
In Lesson03's module <style> block, adopt the treatment Lesson01 already uses for a long title and top-align the pair:
  .hero__inner { align-items: start; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(38px, 5.2vw, 74px); }
This brings the hero to roughly 1150px (in family with L2/L4), removes the void, and puts the objectives card top edge level with the title.

In course.css, cap the running measure so it lands in the 60–75 character band the kit already uses for .prose (720px) and .lede (640px):
  .wrap > p, .wrap > ul, .wrap > ol { max-width: 76ch; }
  .note__body, .tabs__panel > p, .sales-aside p, .widget > p { max-width: 76ch; }
Leave tables, .code-block, figures and grids at full .wrap width.

In course.css, give the heading its own top rhythm:
  .wrap > * + h3, .wrap > * + h4 { margin-top: 40px; }
(40px keeps the 8pt baseline and preserves the existing 8px heading-to-paragraph gap.)

Remove the .btn-row from the recap (see UX-v3-009 — every sibling closes with a p.lede, and the .lesson-nav card directly below already offers Back and Next). If the row is kept, retint it for the dark surface in course.css:
  .review .btn--text { color: var(--veeam-green-bright); }
  .review .btn--text:hover { color: var(--paper); }

course.css line 230:
  .callout strong { color: var(--warn); display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
becomes
  .callout strong { color: var(--warn-text); display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
(--warn-text #8A5500 on --warn-soft measures 5.6:1.) Apply the same substitution to .task__num.is-challenge (course.css:367–369), which repeats the pattern.

Two independent fixes, either sufficient — take both:
1. course.css, so no future long token can break the page: code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
2. Lesson04 #monitor: move the query out of the sentence into the .code-block used for the identical query further down the section, and refer to it in prose by name ("the failed-action query below").

Fix it once in course.css line 281:
  .review-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 40px; }
(5 cards resolve to 3 + 2 at 1440px — no orphan, no empty row.) Then delete the .review-grid rule from Lesson04's module <style> block.

Add to the course.css focus-visible group (lines 142–158) or as its own rule:
  .continue__locked h1:focus-visible,
  .continue__locked h2:focus-visible,
  .continue__locked h3:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--veeam-green-bright);
    outline-offset: 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

Add to the existing max-width:760px media query in course.css:
  .breadcrumb__current { white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; max-width: 46vw; }
or drop the title outright at that width: .breadcrumb__current { display: none; }

Promote the step-down into the kit as one shared modifier rather than a per-module invention, e.g. in course.css:
  .hero h1.hero__title--long { font-size: clamp(38px, 5.2vw, 74px); }
then put class="hero__title--long" on the L1 and L3 H1s and delete L1's module-local .hero h1 rule. One long-title size (74px) instead of 62px on one page and 96px on another.
